I would not make such a blunder.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.000
I see...

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.460
I was born so that I could be a sample
for one of her experiments!

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.670
Well, see ya!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.580
See you tomorrow.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.580
Goodbye.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.380
Chikuwa Bookstore

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.380
I've made up my mind.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.130
I was fine with just looking,

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.210
but if I could actually get to speak with you...

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:44.380
If our eyes could meet as we engaged in talk...

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.580
How brightly this world would shine!

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.420
U-um...!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.040
Just calm down.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.460
I've run through this simulation so many times.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.080
And I have an ace up my sleeve.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.170
That which is needed for a man and woman
who don't know each other to get acquainted...

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.920
Why is my Friend's House

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.170
Yes: Points in common!

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.420
Wh-where did you buy that book?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:18.460
Uh, for... For a while now I've thought,
"That sure looks interesting!"

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.420
I've looked around for it
but I haven't been able to find it.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:26.630
These days you can just buy things online,
so maybe this was a bit of a stretch...

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.790
The Chikuwa Bookstore
at the station's north entrance.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:31.500
If you're that interested in it, I will give it to you.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.080
Sh-she's talking to me!

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:37.500
It would seem the household of
a friend of yours is faced with difficulty.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:40.170
She's really talking to me right now!

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.880
Why is my Friend's House

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.880
Slightly Smelly?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:55.080
True enough, Sasaki kept five hamsters at home,

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:58.380
and Aoyama's house, where you had to pass
through the veranda to get to the bath...

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.210
both of these were slightly smelly.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:04.460
Once I've found my own answer
to this philosophical dilemma,

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:07.130
I will try speaking to you again.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.130
I swear... How bright the setting sun is!

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.500
GRAAARGH!

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:17.500
Hmph!

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.500
Bzzzt

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.040
C'mon, Robo. I said I'm sorry!!

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.040
This cannot be solved by a simple apology.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.290
Let's get along

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.540
Though it may be hard for me to show it,

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:23.790
even I can get hurt.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.080
Now Saginomiya-san and Tanaka-san are fighting?
even I can get hurt.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.790
Now Saginomiya-san and Tanaka-san are fighting?

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.000
S..Saginomiya-san!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.250
P-please wait!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.920
What the heck's going on?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.960
I-It's sort of unusual for you two to be fighting.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:44.710
Saginomiya-san, what happened?

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:47.460
You're always so calm,
so for you to worked up like this...

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.830
Yeah, Robo doesn't get angry that often.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:54.130
She and I don't really get into fights.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.420
But...

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:59.290
Yes. There may have been one time, long ago.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.330
J-just tell me already!

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.710
I can't stand that look you've got on your face!

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:07.710
Please, you can confide in me.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.000
If that will make you feel even a little better, that is.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:16.000
The thing is, Robo, Wota, and I
went to the same elementary school...

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.880
Let's play Cops and Robbers!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.500
I'll be the cop, and Kikuchi and Saginomiya
will be the robbers, okay?!

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.330
Come on! Again?!
We always played together after school,

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:23.880
We always played together after school,

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.750
but Robo ended up going to
a prep school in the next town over.

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:30.500
She may not look it, but she's super smart.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:34.790
Then, when Wota and I went to different classes,
we just fell out of touch.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:38.210
We all led our own lives in middle school...

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.250
but we ran into each other
during the summer of our third year,

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.830
and we started hanging out again.

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:47.920
By that time, Wota and I had
already decided to go to Saijo. Then...

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.920
I will go to Saijo too.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.960
Huh? But you could get into
a much better school, right?

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.880
I have made my decision.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:59.080
What the hell are you thinking?!
Don't throw your life away!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.830
Do not presume to decide my life for me.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.750
That was the first time I'd seen Robo get emotional.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:13.290
I heard later that she was
pretty much alone at school.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:17.040
Like, people couldn't tell what she was thinking,
so they just avoided her.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.540
You need to figure out why she chose Saijo.

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:22.420
But then, Wota stopped talking to me too.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:25.170
We all went our separate ways again.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.540
S-so that's what happened?

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:29.670
That's why I was so happy

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:33.210
when the three of us met again in high school.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.210
1st-year Class Lists

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.830
We're in the same class?!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.000
You're right.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.750
Not to mention, we're in the same grade.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.210
Well of course that's obvious.
Oh, my! What a wonderful story.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:40.750
Oh, my! What a wonderful story.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.250
So, what caused the fight this time?

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.750
The thing is...

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:48.040
After school yesterday, I kinda killed Robo's pet.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.460
That's way too flippant!
Yeah, I kinda messed up!

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:49.960
Yeah, I kinda messed up!

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.330
That's just unacceptable!

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.540
I wouldn't be surprised if she hates you for life!

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:55.960
What? But, you get where I'm going, right?

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.670
When I say "pet," it's the
microorganisms that Robo cultivates.

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:00.710
Microorganisms?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.000
Hey, hey! Robo!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.920
That new comic "Shakure-zamurai"
is super entertaining, so you should read it!

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.130
New serial

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:07.130
Shakure-zamurai

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.130
Oh...!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.790
So, I accidentally smashed it!

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.080
I kinda feel like I've wasted my time listening to this...

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.000
Oh! Robo!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.880
You came back?!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.630
Shakure-zamurai was quite entertaining,
so I will forgive you.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.380
Wasn't it?! I'm looking forward to the next installment!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.460
So, that's what happened.

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:33.040
If it had been me, would I have been able to say
she shouldn't throw her life away?

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.630
I'm ashamed of myself for simply being happy
at the grade-level advancement list...

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.880
There's no end of worry for a girl in love, huh?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:47.380
What I have for Saginomiya-san is respect,
which isn't the same as romantic feelings.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.830
You don't have to try to make it
black and white, you know.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:55.130
A person's feelings are vague
and can fall into, like, gray areas.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.170
You seem like you have some experience with this...

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.880
Because I do have experience.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.710
I've heard a lot of your personal concerns...

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.920
Are you sure you're okay not swearing me to secrecy?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.000
I might accidentally tell someone, you know.

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.790
I don't think you'd say anything, Someya-san...

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.830
Y-you don't know that.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.580
But it's what I want to believe.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.210
A classmate I can share my concerns with...
Someya-san, you may be the first one for me.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.040
Is this what people refer to as "best friends"?

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.920
This! THIS is why you bug me!

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.040
What the hell?! You've got too much potential for this!

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.000
Is this because I went said we might be best friends?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.630
I'm sorry for any bother-

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.790
There! That face!

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.630
You really stir up feminine instincts, you know!

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:40.170
The fact you do it without realizing makes it even
more wicked! Five years in prison for you!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.540
I-I'm sorry...

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.830
See? There's that expression again!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.040
Sorry to have you come all the way out here with me...

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:48.960
It's fine, Takahashi. Do you best out there.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.500
I'll see you at school tomorrow, okay?

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.500
Yeah...

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:53.920
Today, I will definitely get closer to Robo-san.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:56.130
And if things go well, to us being in a relationship...

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.580
I will watch from here and witness your brave stand.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:02.250
After all, I'm your best friend.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.830
So then, that convenience store employee-

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:05.830
Robo-san!

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.960
D-do you remember me?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.210
A guy?!

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.630
You lent me this book a while back.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.290
Yes, I remember you.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:16.500
Do you have a moment?

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:18.420
I wanted to talk to you.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.330
Yes, if it will not take long.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.380
W-well then, we'll just be going now...

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.460
What for?! Let's hear what he has to say!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:25.630
Read between the lines, you idiot!

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:27.540
No! I wanna break this apart!

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.130
I'm not gonna let you get the jump on us, Robo!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:29.710
Get all complicated!

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.000
I-I'm sorry. It looks like you were out with your friends...
Get all complicated!

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.790
I-I'm sorry. It looks like you were out with your friends...
May all your front teeth suddenly fall out!

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:32.290
I-I'm sorry. It looks like you were out with your friends...
May you bite the inside of your cheek

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:32.880
I don't mind. So, what did you want to talk about?
May you bite the inside of your cheek

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.080
I don't mind. So, what did you want to talk about?
and it gets all throbby!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:35.000
I don't mind. So, what did you want to talk about?
Your left and your right cheeks!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:35.880
Um... Th-that is...
Your left and your right cheeks!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.290
Um... Th-that is...

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.170
Me... Me and...

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.330
I can't. When push comes to shove,
I don't have the courage to...

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.330
"Me and"?

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.460
Y-yeah. Me and...

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.130
Me and...

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:50.380
Me and this guy, his name is Aoyama.
We really get along, you see.

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:54.500
He's been my friend since middle school,
and he's a really good guy.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.630
But, the thing is, his house is slightly smelly.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.500
Huh? Wait, me?!
I was wondering why, and when I thought about it,
I came up with about 10 reasons...

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.170
I was wondering why, and when I thought about it,
I came up with about 10 reasons...

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.130
Wh-what the hell am I talking about?

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:05.540
She couldn't possibly be interested in listening to this-

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:06.920
Why don't you tell me about it?

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.630
I can't believe it. She's interested in this?

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.920
The thing is, his house faces north,
and it's got bad ventilation.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:16.540
Plus, there's damp, half-dried laundry
constantly in the room.

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.790
The garbage in the kitchen is in
a constant state of neglect.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:22.920
Also, the shoe cabinet at the front door
is stuffed with old, worn-out shoes.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:24.540
So, that more than meets the necessary definition.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:30.460
Yes! The thing is, I thought about why people
perceive odors like that as being "smelly."

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.000
It's the perception of danger, born from instinct.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.790
Yes! It's an intrinsic function,
for the purpose of avoiding dangerous things.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:39.420
When I think of that, I'm left with one hypothesis:

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:44.630
The smell from Aoyama's house might mean that
I'm rejecting Aoyama on a genetic level!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.130
So, I'm being genetically rejected?

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.500
This could also be the case when seen
from a philosophical viewpoint.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:55.380
Does the smell at Aoyama's house
even actually exist? In other words...

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:58.080
Aoyama's house may not even actually be smelly.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:01.330
It could be that the aversion I feel toward Aoyama
is just making me perceive it that way.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:03.170
He straight-up said "aversion"!

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.500
And what is that aversion?

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.290
Aoyama has a childhood friend, a girl,
and they really get along well.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.920
There might've been a part of me that was jealous,

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:15.250
because he could go in and out of
a girl's room like it was nothing.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.170
Actually, I'm sure of it!

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.580
I see now...

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:23.960
The book you gave me helped me to identify
the negative feelings I've had.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.540
Thank you. Today was about me
wanting to show you my gratitude, so...

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.630
Hey! Why do we have to
take the time to be considerate?

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.420
Still, if she gets a boyfriend,
he might introduce us to his guy friends!

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.880
You... You are smart.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:40.500
If you can get this jealous,
you must like your friend very much.

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:43.210
Aoyama is my number one best friend...

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:44.830
Robo!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.670
H-hey!
I've come to cheer you on!

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.380
I've come to cheer you on!

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:48.500
Takahashi!

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.500
I like you a lot too, Takahashi!

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.630
Takahashi! Takahashi!

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.330
I like you!

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:57.960
I'll lend this to you.
I like you!

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.210
I'll lend this to you.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.580
It's an odor meter, "Smell Sensor-kun."

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.290
I made it to measure a wet dog's odor index,

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:09.290
but it seems like the situation between you two
is more dire, so please use it.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:13.170
You can return it after the facts regarding
your friend's house have been clarified.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:14.670
I shall be waiting.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.460
Hey, Robo! Wait!

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.170
Hey, Robo! Wait!
Never mind our almost smothering friendship,

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:19.580
Hey, wait!
Never mind our almost smothering friendship,

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:20.960
Never mind our almost smothering friendship,

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:25.830
the odor meter, and the slight awkwardness, she left...

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.290
Aw!

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:32.880
What happened to the plan to have him
introduce us to some guys?

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.960
By the way, did you actually like that Takahashi dude?

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:37.420
Well...

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:42.130
If such represents the elation of having found
a candidate for the purpose of

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.290
anti-aging DNA manipulation, then yes.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:46.540
Yasaka Station

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:46.540
Oh!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.960
Teishotoku P has uploaded a new song!

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:51.460
It's that Vocalo P you've been
nuts about from before, right?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:56.330
He's still pretty unknown,
but he must be an awesome guy. I like-

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.830
To say that you "like" him,
when you haven't even met him is just, "Ewe!"

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.330
Shut up! You can get a feel
just by listening to his songs!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.460
If you met him in person, what would you do?

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:05.920
Well, I'd say that I like him, of course!

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:07.000
Eew!

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:12.040
The afternoon song shines, in the corner of the room

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.080
Secret•Sequence

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.080
Teishotoku P here. This is my fifth release.

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.080
I made this when I was gazing at sushi that just passed me by...

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.080
Teishotoku-P-san

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.080
Views

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.080
# of comments

00:20:09.090 --> 00:20:11.080
# in my list

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:11.080
My numbers aren't going up...

00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:17.210
All I do is wait, hoping for the revolution to begin

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:15.920
There was a time I thought
that if I became a famous producer,

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.330
I'd be able to go out with college women.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:22.500
I have to hurry and come up with an answer

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.830
I'm here today again

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:19.830
You do make nice songs

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.830
This song really permeates

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:21.080
No way!

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:22.500
There's no way such a sweet deal could be real!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:27.670
Though I don't know the reason why I should hurry

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.420
At the very least, I'm surrounded by high school girls.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.080
But, no way! I'm glad I don't have one!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.880
I'm free! I don't have to spend money on them!

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:32.290
Regrets, I repeat them and cry

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:31.830
I'm glad I don't have a girlfriend! It's awesome!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:37.460
But I mourn the fact that I can't change

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.750
Soft

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.750
It's nice

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.750
I want the album

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.750
It's lovely

